Third-party material: two carve-outs

The MIT grant above covers this project's own source. It does not and cannot
cover the two bodies of third-party material below. Both are recorded here so
that the limits are visible before anything is ported or published.

Carve-out 1 -- cohem's documentation is not MIT.

  The cohem repository (Paul Chase Dempsey) is the source of the preset-file
  knowledge used by this project. Its README states, verbatim:

      "This repo is nominally MIT-licensed."
      "All graphics and documentation are Copyright (c) Paul Chase Dempsey."

  (ref/cohem/README.md:59 and :64.) The plain-copyright sentence covers
  cohem's Notes.md, which is documentation and therefore outside the MIT
  grant. This project may use the facts Notes.md records -- wire formats,
  message ids, observed behaviour -- but never its prose: no sentence,
  paragraph, table caption or phrasing is copied from it.

  Where cohem's MIT-licensed code is ported into this project, the MIT notice
  and the attribution to Paul Chase Dempsey (full legal name) are carried at
  the ported code itself, not only in this file. MIT-to-MIT is compatible.

Carve-out 2 -- docs/HakenMidi.h is Lippold Haken's copyright
in all three copies: fine privately, a blocker if this repo is ever published.

  The protocol header is the source of truth for every wire format in this
  project and is not this project's to license. The copies present on this
  machine carry the same notice on line 1:

      "// Haken Audio Midi Protocol by Lippold Haken, (C) Copyright 1999-2026."

  The three copies are docs/HakenMidi.h (extracted from the Haken Editor
  install), ref/cohem/include/HakenMidi.h and
  ref/pachde-CHEM/src/em/HakenMidi.h. The header is redistributed by this
  project under no licence at all.

  Consequence: keeping these copies for private use is fine; shipping them, or
  publishing this repository with them in it, is a blocker and needs Lippold
  Haken's permission first. .gitignore already excludes docs/ and ref/, which
  keeps the copies untracked but does not resolve the question.
